This is a list of the tokens that are currently available for use in
MetalScanText. SLTokens must be enclosed in curcly braces {}
(See the chart below and the explanation underneath)


TOKEN              PRINTF DESCRIPTION
                   TYPE
========================================================================
ITEMNUM            (%d)   current item number
POSTDATE           (%s)   item post/upload date
DLOADS             (%d)   number of downloads to current item
RESPS              (%d)   number of downloads
BESTCPS            (%d)   best CPS rate for downloads.
POSTERHANDLE       (%s)   args: 1=realname, 2=handle, default=handle
TOHANDLE           (%s)   args: 1=realname, 2=handle, default=handle
SIZE               (%s)   filesize (displays 0 if not a file adds K or M)
M!UFDP             (%s)   "missing, unvalidated, unfinished, etc,.. flags
TITLE              (%s)   complete filename, not split into root/extension
                          args:  1=all lowercase, 2=all uppercase, 3=don't
                          convert
TITLEROOT          (%s)   root Filename, without the .extension.  CAN be
                          safely used in the "POST" string.. if item is a
                          POST, title will not be altered
TITLEEXT           (%s)   file extension
SUBNAME            (%s)   subboard name
NEWFLAG            (none) flag to show if item has new responses
INFO               (%s)   short file description

*** below are new items for v1.03 ***

RESPNUMBER         (%d)   current response number.
RESPTOTAL          (%d)   number of total responses
RESPNUMOF          (%s)   string comprised of the current response number
                          and the number of TOTAL responses separated by
                          the text "of".
                          ie. 3 of 13
ITEMTOT            (%d)   Number of items total in the current subboard.
BESTCPS            (%d)   Best CPS rate for the current item.
SELECTTITLE        (%s)   The title of the current selection.
SELECTBYTES        (%s)   The size (with K or M added to denote kilo or
                          Mega bytes) of the current selection.
SELECTMAX          (%d)   The maximum number of items that can be selected
                          (ie. the same as your CNet CONFIG/max selections
                           default).
SUBNAME            (%s)   The current subboard title.
MODBREAK           none   This token checks the number of the current item
                          and inserts a NEWLINE (return) based on the
                          "list count" of the current item.  ie. the first
                          item listed/displayed is numbered 0 and the second
                          listed is numbered 1, etc,..  On EVEN numbered
                          items, this return is inserted.

========================================================================

SLToken format: SLTokens accept a printf style specifier after the token
                name.  For programmers, note that any printf style
                formatting specification can be used as long as you keep
                the data TYPE as %s (string).
                For users not familiar with the C language, see below for
                a (simplified) explanation of the fields.  Also look at the
                included MetalScanText to see the format of a printf
                specifier.

 {TITLE %w.ps arg}

    ^    ^ ^^  ^
    |    | ||  additional arguments.  Some tokens may use additional
    |    | ||  arguments, such as the TITLE token.  See above for info
    |    | ||
    |    | |printf conversion specifier:  c=character, s=string, d=integer
    |    | |most SLTokens use "s" for string type.  See above for printf
    |    | |type.
    |    | |
    |    | |
    |    | precision of text display (ie. if "5", restricts the string/digits
    |    | to be 5 characters long
    |    |
    |    Field width to display text in (ie. causes the text to be padded
    |    with extra spaces.
    |
  SLToken name

Note: Tokens are NOT case sensitive.  Use upper/lower or mixed case.
=========================================================================
